---
/**
 * /privacy/
 *
 * PDPA privacy policy. The disclosure-to-vendors section is the one that
 * actually matters for a matching service and is the one most sites in this
 * market gloss over.
 *
 * Placeholders for the DPO contact are rendered visibly rather than hidden, so
 * an unresolved one cannot quietly reach production.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { urls } from '../lib/urls';
import { meta } from '../lib/seo';
import { company, hasUen } from '../lib/data';

const path = urls.privacy();

const { title, description } = meta(
  'Privacy Policy | HomeToClean',
  'How HomeToClean collects, uses and discloses personal data under Singapore PDPA, including disclosure to the vendor partners we match you with.',
);

const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  batch={0}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy Policy', path }]}
>
  <section class="border-b border-line bg-surface">
    <div class="wrap-narrow py-12 sm:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-muted">
        How {company.entityName}, trading as {company.tradingName}, handles your personal
        data under the Singapore Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (PDPA).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-faint">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap-narrow prose-ht py-12 text-ink-muted sm:py-16">
    <div class="rounded-card border border-brand/25 bg-brand-light/50 p-5 text-ink">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="font-semibold">The short version.</strong> We are a matching
        service, not a cleaning company. When you send us an enquiry we pass your name,
        contact details and what you have told us about the job to the cleaning vendors
        matched to your request, so that they can quote you directly. That disclosure is
        the point of the service, and we ask for your consent to it before you submit.
        We do not sell your data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This site is operated by <strong>{company.entityName}</strong>{hasUen() ? ` (UEN ${company.uen})` : ''},
      trading as {company.tradingName}. In this policy, "we", "us" and "our" refer to that
      company.
    </p>
    <p>
      {company.tradingName} is a matching service. We introduce households in Singapore to
      independent cleaning vendors. We do not carry out cleaning work, and we do not
      employ the cleaners who attend your home.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What personal data we collect</h2>
    <p>Through the enquiry form on this site, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name</li>
      <li>Your mobile number and email address</li>
      <li>The service you are asking about, your town and your property type</li>
      <li>How often you want the service and your preferred date</li>
      <li>Anything else you choose to write in the message field</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you email us directly instead, we collect your email address and the contents of
      that correspondence.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also collect basic, non-identifying usage data through Google Analytics, such as
      which pages were viewed and whether an enquiry was started or submitted. We do not
      use this to identify you, and this site does not use browser local storage or session
      storage.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We use your personal data for these purposes, and no others:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>To understand what you need and to respond to your enquiry</li>
      <li>
        To match you with cleaning vendors who cover your area and offer the service you
        asked for, and to pass your enquiry to them so they can quote
      </li>
      <li>To follow up on an enquiry you have made, by email or by telephone if you gave us a number</li>
      <li>To keep records of enquiries, and to improve this site and our matching</li>
      <li>To comply with legal or regulatory obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Disclosure to vendor partners</h2>
    <p>
      This is the disclosure that matters most, so we state it plainly. When you submit an
      enquiry and give consent, we disclose the following to the cleaning vendors matched
      to your request:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, mobile number and email address</li>
      <li>Your town, property type, the service requested, frequency and preferred date</li>
      <li>Any additional details you included in your message</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do this so those vendors can contact you directly and quote. Your enquiry may be
      passed to more than one vendor, so that you can compare. We do not sell personal
      data to anyone, and we do not pass your details to advertisers, data brokers or
      unrelated businesses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once a vendor receives your details, that vendor is a separate organisation with its
      own obligations under the PDPA and its own privacy practices. Any agreement for the
      cleaning work itself is between you and that vendor.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may also disclose personal data to service providers who help us operate this
      site, such as hosting and analytics providers, and where we are required to do so by
      law.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Consent, and withdrawing it</h2>
    <p>
      We ask for your consent on the enquiry form before you submit it. The consent box is
      not ticked by default, and the form cannot be submitted without it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may withdraw your consent at any time by contacting us using the details in
      section 9. We will process the withdrawal within a reasonable period and stop using
      your data for the purposes above. Withdrawing consent does not affect anything done
      before we received the request, and we cannot recall data already disclosed to a
      vendor: you would need to contact that vendor directly.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We retain enquiry data for as long as needed for the purposes set out above, and
      then for up to <strong>24 months</strong> from your last contact with us, so that we
      can deal with follow-up questions and disputes about a job we matched.
    </p>
    <p>
      After that period we delete it or anonymise it, unless we are required to retain it
      longer to meet a legal or accounting obligation.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your right to access and correct</h2>
    <p>Under the PDPA you may ask us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>for access to the personal data we hold about you, and information about how it has been used or disclosed in the past year</li>
      <li>to correct any personal data that is inaccurate or incomplete</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Send the request to the contact in section 9. We will respond as soon as reasonably
      possible. We may need to verify your identity first, and a reasonable fee may apply
      to an access request, as permitted under the PDPA. If we correct your data, we will
      also send the correction to any vendor we disclosed it to in the past year, unless
      that vendor no longer needs it.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Protection of your data</h2>
    <p>
      We make reasonable security arrangements to protect personal data in our possession
      against unauthorised access, collection, use, disclosure, copying, modification or
      disposal. No transmission over the internet can be guaranteed completely secure, and
      we cannot guarantee the security of data you send to us over the internet.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data Protection Officer</h2>
    <p>Questions, access or correction requests, and consent withdrawals go to:</p>
    <div class="rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5 text-sm not-prose">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink">Data Protection Officer</p>
      <p class="mt-1">{company.entityName}</p>
      <p>{company.address.street} {company.address.unit}</p>
      <p>Singapore {company.address.postalCode}</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Contact us through the
        <a href={urls.contact()} class="text-brand underline underline-offset-2">enquiry form</a>,
        marking your message for the attention of the Data Protection Officer. We do not
        publish an inbox address on this site.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows
      when it was last changed. Continuing to use this site after a change means you accept
      the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your personal data, contact our
      Data Protection Officer first. You may also lodge a complaint with the Personal Data
      Protection Commission of Singapore.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm">
      See also our <a href={urls.terms()}>Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
